@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "customer.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Customer Employee Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki employee information transfers properly to customer.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I generate past static start and end dates
	* I generate future static start and end dates
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | cstm.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | cstm.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | CSTM                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                            |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | cstm.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | cstm.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | CSTM                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                            |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | KORCSTKORCST                  | |
	| Name   | Korcst - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |

Teardown:
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| ${staticEmailValue} |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| ${staticEmailValue} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| ${staticEmailValue} |

Scenario: View Liferay employee
	New Liferay employees who are added to koroneiki via okta should sync correctly to Customer

	Given I generate static variables for a support user
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | ${staticScreenNameValue}       |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue}            |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstNameValue} |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastNameValue}  |
	| Group         | Employees                       |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue}" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue}" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue}" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue}" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	And the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue}" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer"
	And the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue}" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - DXP"
	And the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue}" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Portal"
	And the support user with the email address "${staticEmailValue}" should be part of the support organization with the name "Koroneiki Customer - Commerce"
	And I log into the customer homepage as "${staticCustomerAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticCustomerAdminPassword}"